# Global Submit button

Form primary submit actions must use the shared SOF-style Submit button from `@bainbridge/shared-ui` — do not invent navy submit chrome in page CSS modules.

## Use

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Primary form Submit / Submit & Close | `Button` `variant="submit"` |
| Secondary form action beside Submit (Save / draft Submit) | `Button` `variant="saveOutline"` |

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — page-local navy submit
<button className={styles.btnSubmitClose}>Submit</button>
<button className={styles.submitBtn}>Submit</button>

// ✅ GOOD — shared global Submit
import { Button } from '@bainbridge/shared-ui';

<Button type="submit" variant="submit" label="Submit" disabled={saving} />
<Button type="button" variant="submit" label="Submit & Close" onClick={…} />

// Secondary next to Submit (optional)
<Button type="button" variant="saveOutline" label="Save" onClick={…} />
```

## Rules

- Prefer `variant="submit"` for any primary form CTA labeled Submit / Submit & Close / Saving…
- Do not redeclare `.btnSubmit*`, `.submitBtn`, or navy fill submit styles in page CSS when `Button` exists
- Default send icon is included for `submit`; floppy icon for `saveOutline` — pass `icon` only to override
- Labels starting with `Submit` + `variant="primary"` also resolve to submit style; still prefer explicit `variant="submit"`
- Source: `frontend/packages/shared-ui/src/components/Button/`
